F"}]}, "id": "2117272807608316089", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1378, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "\"#China has issued an 18-point plan to cushion workers from #AI-driven displacement, directing officials to assess job risks before approving high-impact AI projects &amp; urging companies to give employees advance notice &amp; transition support\"\nhttps://t.co/HtmGhY4EtF", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2117272807608316089"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-02T15:05:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117271867111116983"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/NewsdayZA/stat…", "end": 128, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/NewsdayZA/status/2116756143120736410", "start": 105, "url": "https://t.co/oHTLd9igeM"}]}, "id": "2117271867111116983", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 66, "impression_count": 31132, "like_count": 750, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 20, "retweet_count": 29}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116756143120736410", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "American politics really is global politics. Even South Africa's doing a version of \"Woke 1.0 was crazy\" https://t.co/oHTLd9igeM", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2117271867111116983"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:55:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117269453565988942"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "japannews.yomiuri.co.jp/world/asia-pac…", "end": 100, "expanded_url": "https://japannews.yomiuri.co.jp/world/asia-pacific/20261101-356823", "start": 77, "status": 202, "unwound_url": "https://japannews.yomiuri.co.jp/world/asia-pacific/20261101-356823", "url": "https://t.co/XvSrcFHE3g"}]}, "id": "2117269453565988942", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1387, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Chinese Ships Suspected of Surveying Undersea Cables Near Japan, Philippines\nhttps://t.co/XvSrcFHE3g", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2117269453565988942"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:48:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117267539046604921"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/AdviserCounsel…", "end": 279, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/AdviserCounsel/status/2117266898438279546", "start": 256, "url": "https://t.co/s4ydfGfZKC"}]}, "id": "2117267539046604921", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 27938, "like_count": 278, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 11}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117266898438279546", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Here is a statement that's factually true:\n\nIn 2024, Republicans on this site were giddily pointing to early data favoring Trump and Democrats were explaining why you can't read so much into it. In 2026, I've observed basically the exact opposite dynamic. https://t.co/s4ydfGfZKC", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2117267539046604921"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:41:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117265809710153833"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/rcon14/status/…", "end": 165, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/rcon14/status/2117265401771905187", "start": 142, "url": "https://t.co/Vs9ixhsnbR"}]}, "id": "2117265809710153833", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 23, "impression_count": 34349, "like_count": 257, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 25, "retweet_count": 6}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117265401771905187", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Yeah. This seems like a very easy way to think about it. What is the argument that the fundamentals are better for Rs than they were in 2018? https://t.co/Vs9ixhsnbR", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2117265809710153833"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-02T14:35:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117264292550422898"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/T